      "content": "     1|# TeamADAPT Prisma Schema Management\n     2|\n     3|## Overview\n     4|DBOps team owns and manages the Prisma schema for all TeamADAPT services. This ensures database consistency and controlled changes across the entire platform.\n     5|\n     6|## Current Status\n     7|✅ **Database:** PostgreSQL 16 on TimescaleDB (port 18030)\n     8|✅ **Schema:** Fully synchronized (60 models from Langfuse)\n     9|✅ **Client:** Generated and available\n    10|✅ **Langfuse:** Connected and operational on localhost:13700\n    11|\n    12|## Directory Structure\n    13|```\n    14|/adaptai/dbops/prisma/\n    15|├── schema.prisma          # Single source of truth for database schema\n    16|├── .env                   # Database connection configuration\n    17|├── manage.sh             # DBOps management script\n    18|└── node_modules/@prisma/  # Generated Prisma Client\n    19|```\n    20|\n    21|## Quick Start\n    22|\n    23|### View Current Status\n    24|```bash\n    25|/adaptai/dbops/prisma/manage.sh status\n    26|```\n    27|\n    28|### Generate Prisma Client (after schema changes)\n    29|```bash\n    30|/adaptai/dbops/prisma/manage.sh generate\n    31|```\n    32|\n    33|### Create New Migration (for schema changes)\n    34|```bash\n    35|/adaptai/dbops/prisma/manage.sh migrate your_change_name\n    36|```\n    37|\n    38|### Deploy to Production\n    39|```bash\n    40|/adaptai/dbops/prisma/manage.sh deploy\n    41|```\n    42|\n    43|### Pull Schema from Database (introspection)\n    44|```bash\n    45|/adaptai/dbops/prisma/manage.sh pull\n    46|```\n    47|\n    48|## Workflow for Schema Changes\n    49|\n    50|### Step 1: Edit Schema\n    51|```bash\n    52|vim /adaptai/dbops/prisma/schema.prisma\n    53|```\n    54|\n    55|### Step 2: Create Migration\n    56|```bash\n    57|cd /adaptai/dbops/prisma\n    58|./manage.sh migrate describe_your_change\n    59|```\n    60|\n    61|### Step 3: Review Migration\n    62|```bash\n    63|ls -la prisma/migrations/\n    64|# Review the SQL in the new migration directory\n    65|```\n    66|\n    67|### Step 4: Test in Development\n    68|```bash\n    69|# If you have a dev database\n    70|npx prisma migrate dev\n    71|```\n    72|\n    73|### Step 5: Deploy to Production\n    74|```bash\n    75|./manage.sh deploy\n    76|```\n    77|\n    78|### Step 6: Generate Updated Client\n    79|```bash\n    80|./manage.sh generate\n    81|```\n    82|\n    83|### Step 7: Notify Service Teams\n    84|Restart any services that use the Prisma client:\n    85|```bash\n    86|sudo systemctl restart langfuse-web langfuse-worker\n    87|```\n    88|\n    89|## Connection Details\n    90|\n    91|### Database\n    92|- **Host:** localhost\n    93|- **Port:** 18030\n    94|- **Database:** teamadapt\n    95|- **User:** postgres_admin_user\n    96|- **Password:** changeme\n    97|\n    98|### Connection String\n    99|```\n   100|postgresql://postgres_admin_user:changeme@localhost:18030/teamadapt\n   101|```\n   102|\n   103|## Schema Information\n   104|\n   105|### Current Models (60 total)\n   106|The database contains a complete Langfuse schema with models including:\n   107|- Users & Organizations\n   108|- Projects & Memberships\n   109|- API Keys\n   110|- Traces & Observations\n   111|- Scores & Evaluations\n   112|- Datasets & Prompts\n   113|- And many more...\n   114|\n   115|### Model Locations\n   116|All Prisma models are defined in: `/adaptai/dbops/prisma/schema.prisma`\n   117|\n   118|## For Application Teams\n   119|\n   120|### Using Prisma Client\n   121|```javascript\n   122|import { PrismaClient } from '@prisma/client'\n   123|\n   124|const prisma = new PrismaClient()\n   125|\n   126|// The client is generated at: /adaptai/dbops/node_modules/@prisma/client\n   127|// Application teams should install: npm install @prisma/client\n   128|\n   129|// Then use in code:\n   130|const users = await prisma.users.findMany()\n   131|```\n   132|\n   133|### Environment Variable\n   134|```bash\n   135|DATABASE_URL=\"postgresql://postgres_admin_user:changeme@localhost:18030/teamadapt\"\n   136|```\n   137|\n   138|### Requesting Schema Changes\n   139|1. Create an issue in TeamADAPT project\n   140|2. Label with: `database`, `schema-change`, `dbops`\n   141|3. DBOps team will review and implement\n   142|4. Changes are deployed via controlled migration process\n   143|\n   144|## Migration History\n   145|\n   146|### Current State\n   147|- Database has 100+ migrations applied\n   148|- All migrations are synced with current schema\n   149|- Schema pulled from production database on 2025-11-20\n   150|- Prisma Client generated: v6.16.2\n   151|\n   152|### Failed Migration\n   153|- `20240419152924_posthog_integration_settings` \n   154|- **Status:** Already applied to database\n   155|- **Action:** No action needed (database is correct)\n   156|- This migration exists in database but not in local migrations folder\n   157|\n   158|## Troubleshooting\n   159|\n   160|### Schema Out of Sync\n   161|```bash\n   162|# Pull latest schema from database\n   163|./manage.sh pull\n   164|\n   165|# Generate client\n   166|./manage.sh generate\n   167|\n   168|# Check status\n   169|./manage.sh status\n   170|```\n   171|\n   172|### Failed Migration\n   173|If a migration fails during deployment:\n   174|```bash\n   175|# Mark as rolled back (if you rolled back manually)\n   176|npx prisma migrate resolve --rolled-back \"migration_name\"\n   177|\n   178|# Mark as applied (if you fixed database manually)\n   179|npx prisma migrate resolve --applied \"migration_name\"\n   180|```\n   181|\n   182|### Permission Issues\n   183|```bash\n   184|# Fix permissions on schema file\n   185|sudo chmod 666 /adaptai/dbops/prisma/schema.prisma\n   186|\n   187|# Fix permissions on management script\n   188|sudo chmod +x /adaptai/dbops/prisma/manage.sh\n   189|```\n   190|\n   191|## Best Practices\n   192|\n   193|### 1. Always Use Management Script\n   194|Don't run `npx prisma` commands directly. Use `./manage.sh` to ensure consistent workflow.\n   195|\n   196|### 2. Review Before Deploying\n   197|Always review migration SQL before deploying to production.\n   198|\n   199|### 3. Coordinate with Teams\n   200|Notify service teams before deploying breaking schema changes.\n   201|\n   202|### 4. Test First\n   203|Test migrations in development before deploying to production.\n   204|\n   205|### 5. Document Changes\n   206|Update this document when making significant schema changes.\n   207|\n   208|## Contact\n   209|- **DBOps Team:** dbops@teamadapt.ai\n   210|- **Slack:** #dbops-critical\n   211|- **On-call:** 24/7 for schema emergencies\n   212|\n   213|## Additional Resources\n   214|- [Prisma Documentation](https://pris.ly/d/documentation)\n   215|- [Prisma Migrate Guide](https://pris.ly/d/migrate)\n   216|- [Schema Reference](https://pris.ly/d/schema-reference)\n   217|\n   218|---\n   219|**Last Updated:** 2025-11-20\n   220|**DBOps Team Ownership:** This schema is owned and managed by TeamADAPT DBOps",
