n    94|- **Timeline**: Phase 2\n    95|- **Criticality**: 10/10 for HITL operations\n    96|\n    97|### 6. ChromaDB (Port 18092)\n    98|- **Technology**: AI-native vector database\n    99|- **Memory**: 500MB\n   100|- **Status**: v0.4.x (hot project)\n   101|- **Use Case**: RAG, embeddings, semantic search\n   102|- **Timeline**: Phase 2\n   103|- **Complements**: Weaviate (both vector DBs, different strengths)\n   104|\n   105|**Phase 2 Total**: +4.5GB RAM → Need cloud scaling\n   106|\n   107|---\n   108|\n   109|## 📊 PHASE 3: Specialized Services (Priority 3)\n   110|\n   111|### 7. DuckDB (Embedded)\n   112|- **Technology**: In-process analytical database\n   113|- **Memory**: Shared with app\n   114|- **Status**: v0.9+ stable\n   115|- **Use Case**: Local analytics, data science notebooks\n   116|- **Timeline**: Phase 3\n   117|\n   118|### 8. OpenSearch (Port 18093)\n   119|- **Technology**: Distributed search & analytics\n   120|- **Memory**: 2GB\n   121|- **Status**: v2.x mature\n   122|- **Use Case**: Full-text search, observability, security analytics\n   123|- **Timeline**: Phase 3\n   124|- **Alternative**: Elasticsearch client already installed\n   125|\n   126|### 9. Dgraph (Ports 18080-18082)\n   127|- **Technology**: Native GraphQL database\n   128|- **Memory**: 2GB\n   129|- **Status**: v21+ stable\n   130|- **Use Case**: Graph APIs, knowledge graphs\n   131|- **Timeline**: Phase 3\n   132|- **Alternative**: Neo4j already configured\n   133|\n   134|---\n   135|\n   136|## 🌊 PHASE 4: Scale & Cloud Migration (Priority 4)\n   137|\n   138|### Cloud-Native Additions\n   139|- **Apache Kafka** (if needed beyond RedPanda)\n   140|- **Apache Cassandra** (wide-column store)\n   141|- **CockroachDB** (cloud-native SQL)\n   142|- **ArangoDB** (multi-model: graph+document+key-value)\n   143|- **Apache Druid** (real-time analytics, alternative to ClickHouse)\n   144|\n   145|### Memory-Optimized Services\n   146|- **Memcached** (port 18071) - Simple distributed cache\n   147|- **Hazelcast** (port 18072) - In-memory data grid\n   148|- **etcd** (port 18079) - Distributed key-value store\n   149|\n   150|---\n   151|\n   152|## 🎯 Strategic Recommendations\n   153|\n   154|### For Laptop (Development/Test)\n   155|✅ **Keep**: Current 10 services + Phase 1 (3 bleeding edge) = **13 services**\n   156|❌ **Avoid**: Phase 2+ (need 16GB+ RAM for comfortable operation)\n   157|\n   158|### For Cloud Servers (Production)\n   159|🚀 **Target**: Full stack (18-22 services)\n   160|- Phase 1 + 2 + 3 = 16 services\n   161|- Each with 2-4GB RAM allocation\n   162|- **Total**: 32-64GB RAM per node\n   163|- **Architecture**: Multi-node clusters for HA\n   164|\n   165|---\n   166|\n   167|## 🔧 Installation Roadmap\n   168|\n   169|### ✅ Completed (Phase 0)\n   170|- [x] DragonflyDB Cluster (3 nodes)\n   171|- [x] Redis Cluster (3 nodes)\n   172|- [x] RedPanda (single node)\n   173|- [x] PostgreSQL\n   174|- [x] Neo4j (configured, needs restart)\n   175|- [x] Weaviate\n   176|- [x] FAISS (Python library)\n   177|- [x] Elasticsearch (Python client)\n   178|- [x] NATS\n   179|\n   180|### 🚧 In Progress (Phase 1)\n   181|- [ ] Materialize (port 18071)\n   182|- [ ] QuestDB (port 18091)\n   183|- [ ] ClickHouse (port 18090)\n   184|\n   185|### 📋 Planned (Phase 2)\n   186|- [ ] Apache Pulsar (ports 18052-18054)\n   187|- [ ] DataHub (port 18085)\n   188|- [ ] ChromaDB (port 18092)\n   189|\n   190|### 📅 Future (Phase 3-4)\n   191|- [ ] DuckDB (embedded)\n   192|- [ ] OpenSearch (port 18093)\n   193|- [ ] Dgraph (ports 18080-18082)\n   194|- [ ] Additional cloud-native services\n   195|\n   196|---\n   197|\n   198|## 💡 Technology Stack Rationale\n   199|\n   200|### Why This组合 (Combo)?\n   201|\n   202|**Real-Time Analytics Trinity**:\n   203|1. Materialize (streaming views) + ClickHouse (OLAP) + QuestDB (TSDB)\n   204|   = Sub-second insights on any data type\n   205|\n   206|**Messaging Layer**:\n   207|- RedPanda (Kafka-compatible) + NATS (cloud-native) + Pulsar (multi-tenant)\n   208|   = Flexibility for different streaming patterns\n   209|\n   210|**Data Models**:\n   211|- PostgreSQL (OLTP) + ClickHouse (OLAP) + Neo4j (Graph) + Weaviate/ChromaDB (Vector)\n   212|   = All major data models covered\n   213|\n   214|**AI/ML Pipeline**:\n   215|- FAISS (local vectors) + Weaviate (managed vectors) + ChromaDB (Python-native)\n   216|   = Complete vector ecosystem\n   217|\n   218|**Observability**:\n   219|- QuestDB (metrics) + PostgreSQL (transactions) + ClickHouse (analytics)\n   220|   = Full system visibility\n   221|\n   222|---\n   223|\n   224|## 🎯 Success Metrics\n   225|\n   226|### Performance Targets\n   227|- **Query Latency**: <100ms for 95th percentile\n   228|- **Ingestion Rate**: 1M events/second (with Pulsar/Kafka)\n   229|- **Storage Efficiency**: 3:1 compression ratio (ClickHouse)\n   230|- **Availability**: 99.9% uptime (multi-node on cloud)\n   231|\n   232|### Developer Experience\n   233|- **One-Command Startup**: All services via systemd/tmux\n   234|- **Local Testing**: Full stack on laptop\n   235|- **Cloud Migration**: Seamless scaling to production\n   236|\n   237|---\n   238|\n   239|## 📚 References & Resources\n   240|\n   241|### Documentation\n   242|- [Materialize Docs](https://materialize.com/docs/)\n   243|- [QuestDB Docs](https://questdb.io/docs/)\n   244|- [ClickHouse Docs](https://clickhouse.com/docs/)\n   245|\n   246|### Community\n   247|- [Materialize Discord](https://discord.gg/MzvvNru)\n   248|- [QuestDB Slack](https://questdb.io/community/)\n   249|- [ClickHouse Community](https://t.me/clickhouse_en)\n   250|\n   251|---\n   252|\n   253|**Next Action**: Install Phase 1 (Bleeding Edge Trio) with laptop-optimized configurations",
