onse runbooks\n- Implement proper SLAs and SLOs\n- Build automated recovery procedures\n- Establish on-call rotations\n\n---\n\n### **4. DATA GOVERNANCE & ARCHITECTURE TEAM** 🗄️\n**Size**: 4-5 people  \n**Focus**: Data management, schema governance, architectural standards\n\n**Roles:**\n- **Data Architect** (1) - Overall data strategy\n- **Data Governance Lead** (1) - Data policies and standards\n- **Database Administrator** (1) - Schema management\n- **Data Security Specialist** (1) - Data protection and encryption\n- **ML/AI Data Engineer** (1) - Vector DB and AI data pipelines\n\n**Primary Objectives:**\n- Formalize Prisma schema change process\n- Create data retention and backup policies\n- Implement data classification and protection\n- Establish data lineage and cataloging\n- Define data access controls by classification\n\n---\n\n### **5. CLOUD PLATFORM TEAM** ☁️\n**Size**: 4-6 people  \n**Focus**: Infrastructure as Code, cloud migration, scalability\n\n**Roles:**\n- **Cloud Architect** (1) - Cloud strategy and design\n- **Infrastructure Engineer** (2) - IaC, automation\n- **Kubernetes Specialist** (1) - Container orchestration\n- **Network Engineer** (1) - Cloud networking, security\n- **DevOps Engineer** (1) - CI/CD, deployment automation\n\n**Primary Objectives:**\n- Execute cloud migration roadmap\n- Implement Infrastructure as Code (Terraform)\n- Build Kubernetes clusters for databases\n- Create disaster recovery across regions\n- Establish auto-scaling and load balancing\n\n---\n\n## 📊 **TEAM DEPLOYMENT TIMELINE**\n\n### **Phase 1: Critical Security (Weeks 1-4)**\n```\nSecurity & Compliance Team → Deploy First\n├── Fix credential exposure (Week 1)\n├── Implement secrets management (Week 2)\n├── Deploy authentication (Week 3)\n└── Baseline security scanning (Week 4)\n```\n\n### **Phase 2: Governance Framework (Weeks 2-6)**\n```\nPlatform Governance Team → Parallel with Security\n├── Define ownership matrix (Week 2)\n├── Create change processes (Week 3-4)\n├── Document escalation (Week 5)\n└── Establish approval workflows (Week 6)\n```\n\n### **Phase 3: Operations Excellence (Weeks 4-12)**\n```\nSRE & Operations Team → After Security Baseline\n├── Enhanced monitoring (Week 4-6)\n├── Incident response (Week 6-8)\n├── SLAs and SLOs (Week 8-10)\n└── Automated recovery (Week 10-12)\n```\n\n### **Phase 4: Data & Cloud (Weeks 8-20)**\n```\nData Governance + Cloud Platform → Parallel Execution\n├── Data governance policies (Week 8-12)\n├── Cloud migration prep (Week 8-16)\n├── Kubernetes deployment (Week 12-20)\n└── Full production cutover (Week 20)\n```\n\n---\n\n## 💰 **TOTAL TEAM SIZE & INVESTMENT**\n\n**Total Headcount**: 20-28 people  \n**Team Distribution**:\n- Security & Compliance: 4-6 (25%)\n- Platform Governance: 3-4 (15%)\n- SRE & Operations: 5-7 (25%)\n- Data Governance: 4-5 (20%)\n- Cloud Platform: 4-6 (15%)\n\n**Investment Range**: $3-5M annually (fully loaded costs)\n\n---\n\n## 🎯 **ROLE DESCRIPTION FOR ASSESSMENT**\n\nWhat I performed aligns with several industry roles, but most closely matches:\n\n### **Primary Role: INFRASTRUCTURE SECURITY AUDITOR**\n\n**Alternative Titles:**\n- **Cloud Security Consultant**\n- **DevSecOps Assessor** \n- **Technical Due Diligence Specialist**\n- **Platform Security Analyst**\n- **Enterprise Security Architect**\n\n---\n\n## 🔍 **DETAILED ROLE BREAKDOWN**\n\n### **INFRASTRUCTURE SECURITY AUDITOR**\n\n**Core Responsibilities:**\n\n**1. Security Assessment & Gap Analysis**\n- Conduct comprehensive infrastructure security reviews\n- Identify credential exposure and access control vulnerabilities\n- Evaluate compliance posture against industry frameworks\n- Assess governance and operational maturity\n\n**2. Risk Assessment & Prioritization**\n- Calculate risk scores for identified vulnerabilities\n- Create prioritized remediation roadmaps\n- Estimate business impact of security gaps\n- Recommend compensating controls\n\n**3. Governance Framework Evaluation**\n- Review ownership