\n- There might be existing ML/AI teams that own this\n\nThe knowledge domain requires specialized ML expertise that goes beyond traditional database management. Incorporating it could dilute the core focus of data architecture, potentially compromising the role's effectiveness. While there's some technical overlap with vector databases and data streaming, the depth of AI/ML knowledge needed suggests maintaining separate specialized teams would be more strategic.\n\nETL integration seems more feasible due to its direct alignment with data pipeline design, streaming technologies, and database systems. This allows for some flexibility without overextending the role's scope."
