              "content": "# AI Agent Security Framework\n\n**Created**: 2025-11-22  \n**Owner**: Tier 2 Data Security Team  \n**Context**: Security for 8,000-10,000 AI agents across 11 domains  \n\n---\n\n## 🎯 **SECURITY PRINCIPLES FOR AI OPERATIONS**\n\n### **1. Zero Trust for AI Agents**\n- **Never trust, always verify** every agent interaction\n- **Micro-segmentation** between agents and domains\n- **Continuous authentication** for all agent activities\n- **Least privilege access** by default\n\n### **2. Domain Isolation**\n- **Complete data separation** between 11 operational domains\n- **Network isolation** via VPCs and security groups\n- **Resource isolation** with quotas and limits\n- **Audit isolation** with separate logging per domain\n\n### **3. AI-Specific Security**\n- **Prompt injection protection** for agent inputs\n- **Model output validation** for harmful content\n- **Agent behavior monitoring** for anomaly detection\n- **Federated learning security** for multi-agent learning\n\n---\n\n## 🏗️ **SECURITY ARCHITECTURE**\n\n### **Multi-Layer Security Model**\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ LAYER 1: NETWORK SECURITY                               │\n│ • VPC isolation per domain                               │\n│ • Zero-trust network architecture                        │\n│ • mTLS for service-to-service                            │\n│ • Network segmentation and micro-segmentation            │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                             │\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ LAYER 2: IDENTITY & ACCESS MANAGEMENT                   │\n│ • Agent identity management                              │\n│ • Role-based access control (RBAC)                       │\n│ • Certificate-based authentication                       │\n│ • Multi-factor authentication for admin access           │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                             │\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ LAYER 3: DATA SECURITY                                  │\n│ • End-to-end encryption                                  │\n│ • Database-level encryption                              │\n│ • Field-level encryption for sensitive data              │\n│ • Secure key management                                  │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                             │\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ LAYER 4: APPLICATION SECURITY                           │\n│ • Input validation and sanitization                      │\n│ • Output filtering and validation                        │\n│ • Secure coding practices                                │\n│ • Runtime application self-protection (RASP)            │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                             │\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ LAYER 5: MONITORING & RESPONSE                          │\n│ • Real-time threat detection                             │\n│ • Behavioral analysis and anomaly detection             │\n│ • Automated incident response                            │\n│ • Forensic analysis and reporting                        │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n## 🔐 **AGENT IDENTITY & AUTHENTICATION**\n\n### **Agent Identity Framework**\n```yaml\nAgent Identity:\n  Agent ID: Unique identifier per agent instance\n  Domain Context: Which domain the agent operates in\n  Trust Level: Security clearance level (1-5)\n  Capabilities: What the agent is authorized to do\n  Constraints: Operational limitations and restrictions\n  \nAuthentication:\n  Method: Certificate-based with PKI infrastructure\n  Rotation: 24-hour certificate rotation\n  Validation: Real-time certificate validation\n  Revocation: Immediate certificate revocation capability\n```\n\n### **Cross-Domain Authentication**\n```yaml\nDomain Boundaries:\n  • Each domain has separate identity provider\n  • Certificate pinning for domain-specific CAs\n  • JWT tokens for cross-domain communication\n  • Token validation at domain boundaries\n\nInter-Domain Communication:\n  • Staged authentication: Agent → Domain → Other Domain\n  • Audit logging for all cross-domain interactions\n  • Rate limiting for cross-domain requests\n  • Content validation at domain boundaries\n```\n\n---\n\n## 📊 **DATA SECURITY STRATEGIES**\n\n### **Encryption at Rest**\n```yaml\nDatabase Encryption:\n  PostgreSQL: Transparent Data Encryption (TDE)\n  MongoDB: Encrypted storage engine\n  ClickHouse: Encrypted disk partitions\n  Redis: Redis Enterprise encryption\n  Qdrant: Collection-level encryption\n\nFile System:\n  • LUKS encryption for all data volumes\n  • Encrypted backups with separate keys\n  • Secure deletion (DoD 5220.22-M standard)\n  • Key rotation every 90 days\n```\n\n### **Encryption in Transit**\n```yaml\nService-to-Service:\n  • TLS 1.3 for all internal communications\n  • Mutual TLS (mTLS) for database connections\n  • Certificate pinning for critical services\n  • Automated certificate renewal (Let's Encrypt)\n\nExternal Communications:\n  • VPN tunnels for management access\n  • IP whitelisting for critical operations\n  • Geographic restrictions where applicable\n  • DDoS protection and rate limiting\n```\n\n### **Field-Level Encryption**\n```yaml\nSensitive Data Types:\n  • Agent memory content (classified information)\n  • Learning data (proprietary algorithms)\n  • Communication logs (privacy-sensitive)\n  • Performance metrics (competitive intelligence)\n\nImplementation:\n  • Application-level encryption before database storage\n  • Separate encryption keys per sensitivity level\n  • Hardware Security Modules (HSMs) for key storage\n  • Encrypted search capabilities (where possible)\n```\n\n---\n\n## 🛡️ **AI-SPECIFIC THREATS & MITIGATIONS**\n\n### **Prompt Injection Attacks**\n```yaml\nThreat:\n  • Malicious inputs designed to override agent instructions\n  • Indirect prompt injection through training data\n  • Social engineering through agent conversations\n\nMitigations:\n  • Input validation and sanitization\n  • Context-aware prompt filtering\n  • Output validation before action execution\n  • Behavior monitoring for anomalous responses\n  • Human review for critical decisions\n```\n\n### **Model Extraction Attacks**\n```yaml\nThreat:\n  • Adversaries attempting to steal AI model parameters\n  • Reverse engineering of agent decision processes\n  • Extraction of training data through queries\n\nMitigations:\n  • Query rate limiting and anomaly detection\n  • Output perturbation to prevent extraction\n  • Differential privacy in model responses\n  • Watermarking for model ownership\n  • Legal protections and monitoring\n```\n\n### **Data Poisoning**\n```yaml\nThreat:\n  • Malicious data injection into training sets\n  • Corrupted agent memory and learned behaviors\n  • Adversarial examples in agent interactions\n\nMitigations:\n  • Data validation and integrity checks\n  • Ensemble models for consensus validation\n  • Continuous monitoring for data anomalies\n  • Automated rollback for corrupted learning\n  • Human oversight for critical learning updates\n```\n\n---\n\n## 🔍 **MONITORING & DETECTION**\n\n### **Behavioral Analysis**\n```yaml\nAgent Behavior Monitoring:\n  • Normal behavior baselines per agent\n  • Anomaly detection using ML models\n  • Real-time alerts for suspicious activities\n  • Historical behavior analysis for patterns\n\nCross-Agent Monitoring:\n  • Communication pattern analysis\n  • Resource usage anomaly detection\n  • Unauthorized data access attempts\n  • Coordination attack detection\n```\n\n### **Real-Time Threat Detection**\n```yaml\nNetwork Monitoring:\n  • Traffic analysis for malicious patterns\n  • Intrusion detection systems (IDS)\n  • Network flow analysis and correlation\n  • Geographic anomaly detection\n\nApplication Monitoring:\n  • Application Performance Monitoring (APM)\n  • Security Information and Event Management (SIEM)\n  • User and Entity Behavior Analytics (UEBA)\n  • Threat intelligence integration\n```\n\n### **Incident Response**\n```yaml\nAutomated Response:\n  • Immediate agent isolation for suspicious behavior\n  • Automatic certificate revocation\n  • Traffic filtering for compromised agents\n  • Database access restriction\n\nHuman Response:\n  • Security team notification\n  • Forensic investigation procedures\n  • Compliance reporting requirements\n  • Recovery and remediation planning\n```\n\n---\n\n## 📋 **COMPLIANCE FRAMEWORKS**\n\n### **SOC 2 Type II Compliance**\n```yaml\nSecurity (CC):\n  • Access controls and authentication\n  • Network security and segmentation\n  • Data encryption and protection\n  • Incident response procedures\n\nAvailability (A):\n  • System monitoring and alerting\n  • Disaster recovery planning\n  • Capacity planning and scaling\n  • Performance monitoring\n\nConfidentiality (C):\n  • Data classification and handling\n  • Encryption and key management\n  • Access logging and monitoring\n  • Secure disposal procedures\n```\n\n### **GDPR Compliance**\n```yaml\nData Subject Rights:\n  • Right to access (data portability)\n  • Right to rectification (data correction)\n  • Right to erasure (right to be forgotten)\n  • Right to restrict processing\n\nPrivacy by Design:\n  • Data minimization principles\n  • Purpose limitation for data usage\n  • Consent management for AI learning\n  • Data protection impact assessments\n```\n\n### **AI-Specific Regulations**\n```yaml\nAlgorithmic Accountability:\n  • Model transparency and explainability\n  • Bias detection and mitigation\n  • Human oversight for critical decisions\n  • Audit trails for AI decision-making\n\nEthical AI Guidelines:\n  • Fairness in agent interactions\n  • Transparency in AI operations\n  • Accountability for AI actions\n  • Privacy protection for AI users\n```\n\n---\n\n## 🔧 **IMPLEMENTATION CHECKLIST**\n\n### **Security Infrastructure Setup**\n- [ ] Deploy zero-trust network architecture\n- [ ] Implement certificate-based authentication\n- [ ] Configure domain isolation (11 domains)\n- [ ] Set up centralized logging and monitoring\n- [ ] Deploy intrusion detection systems\n- [ ] Configure automated threat response\n\n### **Data Protection Implementation**\n- [ ] Enable encryption at rest for all databases\n- [ ] Configure TLS for all data in transit\n- [ ] Implement field-level encryption for sensitive data\n- [ ] Set up key management and rotation\n- [ ] Configure secure backup procedures\n- [ ] Test data recovery and restoration\n\n### **AI-Specific Security Measures**\n- [ ] Implement prompt injection protection\n- [ ] Deploy model output validation\n- [ ] Set up agent behavior monitoring\n- [ ] Configure anomaly detection systems\n- [ ] Implement federated learning security\n- [ ] Deploy adversarial example detection\n\n### **Compliance & Governance**\n- [ ] Establish data classification framework\n- [ ] Implement access control policies\n- [ ] Configure audit logging for all activities\n- [ ] Set up compliance reporting automation\n- [ ] Establish incident response procedures\n- [ ] Deploy security training programs\n\n---\n\n## 📚 **SECURITY TOOLS & TECHNOLOGIES**\n\n### **Network Security**\n- **Firewall**: Palo Alto Networks / Cisco ASA\n- **IDS/IPS**: Suricata / Snort\n- **VPN**: OpenVPN / WireGuard\n- **Network Monitoring**: Zeek / Wireshark\n\n### **Identity & Access Management**\n- **PKI**: HashiCorp Vault / AWS Certificate Manager\n- **IAM**: Keycloak / AWS IAM\n- **MFA**: Duo / YubiKey\n- **Secrets Management**: HashiCorp Vault / AWS Secrets Manager\n\n### **Database Security**\n- **Encryption**: Transparent Data Encryption (TDE)\n- **Access Control**: Database-native RBAC\n- **Audit Logging**: Database audit extensions\n- **Backup Encryption**: Encrypted backup solutions\n\n### **Monitoring & SIEM**\n- **SIEM**: Splunk / ELK Stack / Graylog\n- **APM**: Datadog / New Relic / Prometheus\n- **Network Monitoring**: Nagios / Zabbix\n- **Log Management**: ELK / Splunk / Fluentd\n\n---\n\n## 🚨 **INCIDENT RESPONSE PROCEDURES**\n\n### **Security Incident Classification**\n```yaml\nCritical (P0):\n  • Data breach or exfiltration\n  • Complete system compromise\n  • Active attacker presence\n  • Service completely unavailable\n\nHigh (P1):\n  • Partial system compromise\n  • Unauthorized access attempts\n  • Malware detection\n  • Significant service degradation\n\nMedium (P2):\n  • Policy violations\n  • Suspicious activity\n  • Performance anomalies\n  • Configuration drift\n\nLow (P3):\n  • Security warnings\n  • Minor policy violations\n  • Routine security events\n  • Informational alerts\n```\n\n### **Response Timeline**\n```yaml\nCritical (P0):\n  • Immediate: Agent isolation and system lockdown\n  • 15 minutes: Security team notification\n  • 1 hour: Executive notification\n  • 4 hours: Initial containment complete\n  • 24 hours: Root cause analysis begin\n\nHigh (P1):\n  • 30 minutes: Initial assessment\n  • 1 hour: Containment measures deployed\n  • 4 hours: Incident team assembled\n  • 24 hours: Investigation complete\n  • 72 hours: Remediation complete\n\nMedium (P2):\n  • 2 hours: Initial assessment\n  • 8 hours: Investigation begin\n  • 24 hours: Resolution implemented\n  • 1 week: Post-incident review\n\nLow (P3):\n  • 1 business day: Assessment\n  • 3 business days: Investigation\n  • 1 week: Resolution\n  • 2 weeks: Documentation\n```\n\n---\n\n## 📊 **SECURITY METRICS & KPIs**\n\n### **Operational Security Metrics**\n- **Mean Time to Detection (MTTD)**: <5 minutes for critical threats\n- **Mean Time to Response (MTTR)**: <15 minutes for critical incidents\n- **False Positive Rate**: <5% for security alerts\n- **Security Patch Compliance**: 100% within 30 days\n- **Certificate Expiry Rate**: 0% (automated renewal)\n\n### **Compliance Metrics**\n- **SOC 2 Compliance Score**: >95%\n- **GDPR Compliance Score**: >98%\n- **Security Training Completion**: 100%\n- **Audit Finding Resolution**: <30 days\n- **Access Review Completion**: Quarterly, 100%\n\n### **Business Impact Metrics**\n- **Security Incident Business Impact**: <1 hour downtime/month\n- **Cost of Security Incidents**: <0.1% of revenue\n- **Security Investment ROI**: Positive within 12 months\n- **Customer Trust Score**: >90% satisfaction with security\n\n---\n\n*This security framework provides comprehensive protection for AdaptAI's agent operations while maintaining the agility and scalability required for AI-scale infrastructure.*\n",
